-- What's new: the latest versions' notes for the settings panel.
-- GENERATED by tools/changelog2lua.js from CHANGELOG.md; do not edit by hand.
local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "7.1", text = "A big tidy-up of the settings: fewer rows, clearer names and a smarter Info Panel. Plus a batch of fixes from Discord.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating.|r This version adds a new file, and a /reload doesn't load it.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffForever Style, rogues and druids:|r build combo points on a target. They should show round the target's portrait.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode:|r open any unit frame. Check the new |cffffffffIcons|r, |cffffffffBar Effects|r and cast bar |cffffffffShow|r lists.\n• |cffffffffFriendly Name Only plates with Show Target's Plate:|r target a player, then clear the target. The name should show once, every time.\n• |cffffffffDruids with Keep Page 1 > On Shapeshift:|r go into Cat and Bear Form. Action Bar 1 should stay on its first page.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things change even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Click-Through:|r now one setting for all plates. If you had it on for any plate type, it's now on for all of them.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Name Only Mode:|r no longer greys out the other options. Show Plates in Combat and Show Target's Plate still give the plate its bar.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Crowd Control and Defensives:|r their icons use the Auras look. Their own Aura Icon Shape, Aura Swipe and Aura Timer are gone.\n• |cffffffffForever Style:|r the name box always shows the full name, as on Blizzard's frames. Show Name is gone from Forever Style.\n• |cffffffffSwing bars:|r Waiting State, Queued Attack Colour and Stand-Still Zone are always on.\n• |cffffffffSwing bars, Off-Hand Swing:|r shows only with a weapon in your off hand.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r finished quests always show \"(Complete)\".\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders:|r the In Dungeons and In Raids timings are gone. Remind Before It Ends counts everywhere.\n• |cffffffffGryphons:|r now part of Quality of Life. They work with Action Bars off, and go back to Blizzard's with Quality of Life off.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffInfo Panel:|r a small grey line under each option's title shows its default, whether it needs a reload, and what it needs to be on (in orange while that greys it out). Choice names in lists are gold, and every description was rewritten to be shorter and clearer.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode, unit frames:|r related switches are now one dropdown each, on every frame:\n      - |cffffffffBar Effects:|r Bar Animations, Bar Edge Glow, Damage Trail\n      - |cffffffffIcons:|r resting, leader, PvP, ready check, raid markers and the rest, now in Look\n      - |cffffffffShow|r (cast bars): Icon, Spell Timer, Centred Spell Name, Edge Glow, Latency, Spell Pushback\n      - |cffffffffText|r (swing, flight, seal and duration bars): Name, Timer, Icon\n• |cffffffffCopy Look to All Frames:|r a button in each unit frame's Edit Mode window. It copies that frame's Bar Texture, Border, Absorb Texture, Background, Class Colours and Bar Effects to every other frame.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• Party: cast bar |cffffffffPosition|r (Above or Below). Auras on that side move past it.\n• Flag carriers: |cffffffffRange Check|r (off) and, in Modern Style, |cffffffffPortrait|r (None or Class Icon).\n• Main tank targets: |cffffffffTarget Border|r and |cffffffffShow Target Markers|r, as on party targets.\n• Pet: |cffffffffThreat Glow|r in every style, the simple pet frame too.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• Health, power and mana bars: |cffffffffValues on Mouseover|r.\n• Druid Mana: |cffffffffIn Caster Form|r is now a choice in its |cffffffffVisibility|r list.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Name Only Mode: |cffffffffShow Level|r, the level in front of the name.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• |cffffffffKeep Page 1|r gets |cffffffffOn Shapeshift|r for druids' Cat and Bear Form (off).\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffBorder:|r your Shared Media borders, under a line below FlareUI Thick. They may not line up with the map's edge.\n• Round minimap: with |cffffffffBelow the Map|r on, the Info Bar can use all three cells.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Settings, merged into one dropdown each|r\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffKeep Page 1|r (In Stealth, In Stances, On Shapeshift) and Fake Cooldown Manager |cffffffffBars|r.\n• Nameplates: |cffffffffTarget Highlight|r, |cffffffffThreat Effects|r, |cffffffffQuest Marks|r (Icon, Progress), |cffffffffKick Ready|r (Colour, Mark), |cffffffffGroup Colours|r (Party, Raid) and |cffffffffUnder the Name|r (Title, Guild).\n• Meters: |cffffffffPull Warning|r (Flash, Sound; the sound can play on its own now) and |cffffffffAuto Reset|r.\n• Chat: |cffffffffNames|r (Better Player Names, Better NPC Names, Level Before Names).\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffGuild|r (Off, Name, Name and Rank).\n• General: |cffffffffLanguage|r, with Game Language first.\n• Bags & Looting: |cffffffffLoot Window|r (Off, Grow Down, Grow Up). Elixirs: |cffffffffAll in Your Bags|r is now the top choice of |cffffffffElixirs and More|r.\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffRumble|r (Alerts, Procs). Buff Reminders: |cffffffffHide|r (In Rested Areas, While Mounted) in Edit Mode.\n\n|cffe6cc99Settings, moved and renamed|r\n• Quality of Life: Extras and Systems are one |cffffffffExtras|r tab. General: the General tab is now |cffffffffAccount|r, and fonts are split into |cffffffffGlobal Font|r and |cffffffffGame Fonts|r.\n• |cffffffffFake CM|r is now |cffffffffFake Cooldown Manager|r everywhere. Its note says why you'd use it over Blizzard's.\n• Sizes in % are now |cffffffffScale|r (Combat Text, Drawer Button, Name Only, Level Disc).\n• Nameplate Font is now |cffffffffWorld Names Font|r: it sets the names over characters in the world and on Blizzard's nameplates.\n• Nameplates: Health Text is |cffffffffBar Text|r, Threat Percentage is |cffffffffThreat Text|r. Show Plates in Combat moved to Visibility.\n• Tooltips: Coloured Borders and Class-Coloured Names moved to the first tab.\n• Raid: the group order row is now |cffffffffGroup Order|r, and Groups is |cffffffffOrientation|r.\n• Many smaller regroups, so every section reads in the same order.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffBar Text|r on mirrored frames: Left and Right in the menu are now the screen's sides. Your frames look the same as before.\n• Edit Mode: |cffffffffCombo Points|r moved to Look. Opacity on Buff Reminders moved to Fading.\n\n|cffe6cc99Removed|r\n• Pet: |cffffffffOnly My Debuffs|r (it only emptied the list).\n• Target and target of target: |cffffffffHas a Target|r in Visibility (always true on those frames).\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• Forever Style: combo points didn't show on the target frame.\n• The player frame's |cffffffffCast Name|r and |cffffffffSpell Timer|r fonts showed while the Player Cast Bar was on, though they don't style it. They now hide then; the bar's fonts are under |cffffffffPlayer Cast Bar|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Friendly Name Only plates with |cffffffffShow Target's Plate|r and |cffffffffNames Above Plate|r: the name went missing on your target and showed twice after.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• The |cffffffffFlareUI Minimap Button|r switch was greyed out with Drawer Style Off.\n\n|cffe6cc99Edit Mode|r\n• Raid: two rows were called Sort By.\n• Loot Rolls: |cffffffffFaded Opacity|r showed above the switch that turns it on." },
    { version = "7.0.18", text = "Dragons for Modern frames, and the end of blocked bag items (we hope, for real this time).\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating.|r This version brings new art files, and a /reload doesn't load them.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffBags:|r visit the guild bank, then your bank. Afterwards, right-click a potion or a recipe in your bags. It should work.\n• |cffffffffDruids:|r fly from Moonglade to Rut'theran twice. The second flight should count down.\n• |cffffffffPortrait > Class Icon:|r target an enemy player. You should see their class icon, not their face.\n• |cffffffffCast bar with Edge Glow:|r get a cast interrupted. The glow should go away with the cast.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things change even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffBags:|r FlareUI no longer opens your bags with the guild bank. Press B to open them there.\n• |cffffffffOpen with Character Window|r is gone from Bags & Looting. Your bags no longer open with the character window.\n• |cffffffffModern frames:|r elites, rares and bosses no longer get a gold or silver border. The border stays bronze, and a dragon shows instead (see Changed).\n• |cffffffffModern boss frames and flag carriers|r start a few pixels further left. Only if you never moved them.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• Target of Target and Target of Focus: |cffffffffPortrait|r (2D or Class Icon) in Edit Mode, in FlareUI Style and Forever Style, with |cffffffffSimple Target of Target|r off.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• Modern, |cffffffffElite & Rare|r icon: Blizzard's dragon now wraps around the outer end of the target, focus and boss frames, instead of the skull.\n      - Gold for elites\n      - Silver for rares\n      - Gold with wings for bosses\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• Items in your bags could not be used after a bank visit, until you typed /reload. The cause was FlareUI opening your bags for the guild bank or the character window.\n• Buying a bank tab or a guild bank tab was blocked after the same visits.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffPortrait > Class Icon|r showed the 2D picture on enemy players.\n• Cast bars: |cffffffffEdge Glow|r stayed on the bar after a cast was interrupted or failed.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• IM chat style: with |cffffffffEdit Box Position|r Above or Below, the chat box disappeared when you stopped typing. It now stays, faint and clickable, as in Blizzard's IM style. Inside works as before.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• |cffffffffFlight Timer:|r the druid flight from Moonglade never counted down. It is now learned like any other flight." },
    { version = "7.0.17", text = "New unit frame art, a combat ring you can't miss, and a pile of fixes from Discord and GitHub.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating.|r This version brings new art files, and a /reload doesn't load them.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffCombat:|r start a fight. The ring around your portrait flares, then stays red. In Forever Style, your name box turns red too.\n• |cffffffffHunters:|r fight in melee range. Your nameplates and frames should stay fully visible.\n• |cffffffffRange Check as a warrior, hunter or Bear Form druid:|r step out of range. The target's frame should fade.\n• |cffffffffDruids:|r fly from Moonglade to Rut'theran. The Flight Timer should know the flight the next time.\n• |cffffffffBattlegrounds:|r the PvP icon shows on your frame and your party's.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look different even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffTarget Highlight > Bar:|r it brightens your target's bar instead of colouring it. Its colour is gone from Pick Your Colours.\n• |cffffffffParty Members|r nameplate colour is mint green, so it no longer looks like a mage's or a shaman's.\n• |cffffffffSquare minimap with Border: Header:|r the frame is 16 px taller at the bottom, so the map starts under the title bar.\n• |cffffffffPlayer Cast Bar:|r |cffffffffWidth|r now counts the icon. Your bar keeps its size. The default is 275.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffShow Latency|r (on): the end of the cast bar shows your latency. In the Player Cast Bar's Behaviour section and in the player frame's Cast Bar section.\n• With Plumber installed, clicking your pet's happiness face opens Plumber's pet food menu.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffShow Target's Plate|r (off) for Name Only Mode: your target gets its full plate back. Set per unit type.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• |cffffffffBar Edge Glow|r (off) on the power and mana bars.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buffs & Debuffs|r\n• Totems: |cffffffffAura Icon Shape|r (Round).\n\n|cffe6cc99Cooldown Manager|r\n• Tracked Bars, in Edit Mode, with Growth Up or Down:\n      - |cffffffffSort By|r (Blizzard): Blizzard, Newest First or Newest Last\n      - |cffffffffMax Bars|r (20)\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• |cffffffffSort By:|r a new choice, By Zone and Level.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• |cffffffffGreater Blessings|r (off) in the Blessing reminder's menu.\n\n|cffe6cc99Fading|r\n• |cffffffffOpacity|r (100) under Faded Opacity, in every Visibility Fading section: how visible the frame is when it isn't faded.\n\n|cffe6cc99For addon authors|r\n• |cffffffffFlareUI_QuestTrackerAPI:|r place your own buttons beside the quest tracker's rows. See API.md on GitHub.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• New ring and plate art:\n      - The portrait sits in the middle of its ring.\n      - FlareUI Style: the whole ring and its shadow show, and the level lines up with the bars.\n      - Forever Style: the bars sit inside the plate's slots.\n• |cffffffffCombat Glow:|r\n      - When a fight starts, the ring gives two quick, bright pulses.\n      - During the fight it stays clearly red and never fades out.\n      - Forever Style: your name box turns red and pulses with it.\n• Forever Style party: |cffffffffShow Name|r is a choice now: Off, First Name, Last Name or Full Name.\n• |cffffffffPlayer Cast Bar:|r |cffffffffWidth|r counts the icon. By Nico-Mayer.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• New quest mark art. It sits 2 px from the plate.\n• The threat box uses your target's border colour and Outer Glow.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Food and Flask is now |cffffffffConsumables to Watch|r: None, Food, Flask, Elixirs.\n• |cffffffffElixirs and More|r lists elixirs by what they give. Your ticks are kept.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• French updated. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift:|r the left text hid behind the portrait in FlareUI Style.\n• The PvP icon didn't show in battlegrounds, on unit and party frames.\n• |cffffffffRange Check:|r warriors, hunters and Bear Form druids were always in range. The spells it used, such as Heroic Strike, count at any distance.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Hunters: plates and frames faded when the target was close.\n• The quest mark was stretched.\n• |cffffffffColour Mob Types > Caster|r didn't work in dungeons.\n• |cffffffffParty Colour|r and |cffffffffRaid Colour|r turned grey in Name Only Mode.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• The XP bar went under the minimap after you clicked it.\n• |cffffffffSquare minimap with Border: Header:|r the map sat under the title bar.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Custom reminders: unticking one could remove another.\n• |cffffffffPet to Summon > Last Used:|r the pet you already had out didn't count.\n\n|cffe6cc99Flight Timer|r\n• Flights started by talking to someone, such as Moonglade to Rut'theran, were never learned.\n\n|cffe6cc99Move Any Window|r\n• With TSM, Blizzard's profession window popped onto the screen." },
    { version = "7.0.16", text = "Aura corners that use the whole frame, a threat number that knows you're the tank, and a long list of fixes.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffDispel icons:|r a friend with a Magic, Curse, Disease or Poison debuff shows the icon. Enemies never do.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage:|r tank a few mobs in a group. The ones you hold are green, the ones you lost are red.\n• |cffffffffBuffs and debuffs Above or Below the Frame, or in one corner only:|r smaller icons or a wider frame fit more on a line.\n• |cffffffffMeter:|r use Create a New Tab, then check the new tab's list in a fight.\n• |cffffffffLoot window:|r Growth on Up, then drag the window and loot again.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look different even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffBuffs and debuffs in a corner:|r with nothing in the corner across from them, they use the whole width of the frame.\n• |cffffffffCooldown Manager:|r the Essential and Utility icons and Tracked Buffs fill from the middle. Pick another |cffffffffGrowth|r in Edit Mode to change it.\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r the name colours from before 7.0.15 are back.\n• |cffffffffSkin Item Slots:|r Colour by Rarity starts at green. Grey and white items have the bronze border.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage:|r its colours follow your Role.\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed and loot rolls:|r they show above the bags and other windows.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffCenter Spell Name|r (off): the spell's name in the middle of the cast bar.\n      - In Edit Mode, in every frame's Cast Bar section\n      - For the Player Cast Bar, in its Look section\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Crowd control and defensive icons have their own |cffffffffAura Icon Shape|r, |cffffffffAura Swipe|r and |cffffffffAura Timer|r. Until you pick something, they follow the other auras.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r |cffffffffGrowth|r (Down) and |cffffffffRow Order|r (Top to Bottom). By Xentinus.\n• |cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack:|r each soul bag in your bag slots gets its own section.\n\n|cffe6cc99Cooldown Manager|r\n• |cffffffffGrowth|r (From the Middle) for the Essential and Utility icons, in Edit Mode.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffInfo Bar:|r Friends and Guild. They count who is online. Point at them to see who.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r colours:\n      - Tank: green while you hold the mob, orange when you're losing it, red when you lost it\n      - Damage & Healer: green while you're safe, red when it's on you\n      - The green is your |cffffffffYou Hold It|r colour\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r names have FlareUI's colours again, and titles and guilds have a colour of their own.\n• The target arrows push the quest mark and the other marks beside the plate out of the way.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffShow Spell Pushback|r comes after Edge Glow.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffReverse Bag Fill|r works with Category Rows. Each section fills that way under its header.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• The gear menu's Show New Window is now called |cffffffffCreate a New Tab|r, because that's what it does.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• |cffffffffZone Headings|r greys out with Sort By on By Level or By Progress, where there are no headings.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Pet Reminders are for a missing or dead pet. The one for a hurt pet never showed, so it's gone.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• A Lua error with buffs and debuffs in places that share an edge, such as Above the Frame and Above the Frame, Left.\n• Buffs and debuffs in a corner wrapped at the middle of the frame, even with nothing in the other corner.\n• Dispel icons showed where you can't dispel:\n      - Players of the other faction who aren't flagged for PvP\n      - Bleeds\n      - Party and raid members under Mind Control\n• |cffffffffThreat Text:|r 0% on a mob only you have threat on, where the game hides the numbers.\n• The interrupt colour counted an interrupt your stance or shield didn't allow.\n• \"Interrupted by\" stayed on the cast bar for your next target.\n• |cffffffffName Above Frames:|r names in other alphabets showed as boxes.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Rows of buffs and debuffs fit one icon less since 7.0.9.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage:|r a red 0% on a mob only you have threat on, where the game hides the numbers.\n• A plate reused in a fight could show dispel icons on an enemy.\n• Plates kept the wrong type when you changed sides, as in a duel.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• |cffffffffUpdate Spell Ranks|r left out the controller bars.\n• The range colours also changed buttons that aren't FlareUI's.\n• |cffffffffSharp Outline:|r text that stayed on screen after its bar faded out should go now. We couldn't see it ourselves, so tell us if it stays.\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menu|r\n• Party buttons kept old names after the group changed in a fight.\n• Some spell ranks were wrong right after logging in.\n• Party spells in a sub-radial now spread over your group.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• The separate threat window didn't follow the meter's Opacity.\n• Pointing at the separate threat window didn't bring back a faded meter.\n• |cffffffffBar Texture:|r it could go back to Blizzard's after a while. We couldn't find the cause, but it now puts itself right.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• Share Quest could be blocked when a fight started with the menu open.\n• Item buttons could use the wrong quest's item, and took clicks while faded out.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• A farming HUD that takes the map no longer gets our click area, fading and hidden dots.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Short buffs counted as running out too early, such as Battle Shout.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• Accept Summons no longer takes a summons out of the starting area or into a scenario. You answer those.\n\n|cffe6cc99Languages|r\n• |cffffffffHungarian:|r two lines had wrong letters. By Xentinus." },
    { version = "7.0.15", text = "A hotfix for the Lua error when you change target in a fight (our own doing, from 7.0.14), plus a few fixes and small additions.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffDispel icons:|r change target in a fight with debuffs up. Friends show the icons, enemies don't.\n• |cffffffffRaid Manager:|r join a group in and out of a fight, with it hidden.\n• |cffffffffDruids:|r |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r with Smooth Animated Bars.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the colours in |cffffffffName Only Mode|r.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look different even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r titles and guilds take the name's colour, and names take the colours Blizzard gives them. Colours you picked yourself stay.\n• |cffffffffRaid Manager:|r if you hid it but play without our Action Bars, it's hidden now.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r with a font picked for Item Level, the BoE mark takes it too.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffCopy From|r, in Plate Setup: puts another unit's whole setup on the one you're editing. Undo Changes takes it back.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffName Only Mode:|r Blizzard's colours for names, titles and guilds.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffOnly Mana Power Bars|r (off) works in every party style, Forever Style too.\n• A |cffffffffFrame Style|r you pick waits for the reload. By mateuszmalek.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• The BoE mark takes the Item Level font, in the bags and the loot window.\n\n|cffe6cc99Languages|r\n• |cffffffffRussian:|r shorter names for the Nameplates tabs and Plate Setup.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• A Lua error each time you changed target in a fight.\n• The player and target frames got shorter when you switched |cffffffffFrame Style|r and back. By mateuszmalek.\n• |cffffffffSmooth Animated Bars|r left out the |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r bar.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• The target arrows hitched at each end of their bounce.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quality of Life|r\n• A hidden |cffffffffRaid Manager|r still showed with Action Bars off, or when you joined a group in a fight." },
}
